---
layout: null
---
{%- comment -%}
The search index, built at deploy time from the same _data files the page
renders from. No plugin: GitHub Pages runs Jekyll in safe mode, so anything
that needs a gem is out. jsonify does the escaping; strip_html means the index
holds what a reader sees, not the markup around it.

Fields are one letter because this file ships to every visitor who opens the
box, and the names repeat once per entry.
  t title   s section   u url   b body
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture bio %}{% include section-biography.html %}{% endcapture -%}
[
{
"t": "About Me",
"s": "Bio",
"u": {{ "/#biography" | relative_url | jsonify }},
"b": {{ bio | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }}
}
{%- for n in site.data.news %},
{
"t": {{ n.body | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncate: 90 | jsonify }},
"s": {{ n.label | append: " · News" | jsonify }},
"u": {{ "/#news" | relative_url | jsonify }},
"b": {{ n.body | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }}
}
{%- endfor %}
{%- assign cards = site.data.publications | concat: site.data.projects %}
{%- for c in cards %},
{
"t": {{ c.title | strip_html | jsonify }},
"s": "Research",
"u": {{ "/#" | append: c.slug | relative_url | jsonify }},
"b": {{ c.authors | append: " " | append: c.venue | append: " " | append: c.summary | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }}
}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for s in site.data.service %},
{
"t": {{ s | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncate: 90 | jsonify }},
"s": "Academic Service",
"u": {{ "/service/#reviewer" | relative_url | jsonify }},
"b": {{ s | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }}
}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for i in site.data.profile.interests %},
{
"t": {{ i | jsonify }},
"s": "Research interest",
"u": {{ "/#biography" | relative_url | jsonify }},
"b": {{ i | jsonify }}
}
{%- endfor %}
]
